# =====================================================================
#  UserSearchesTree.ab
# =====================================================================
#  sentence   User Search Tree
#  v4         $('#search') input listener  — IMPLEMENTED
#             leftpanel_v4.html lines 872-875.
#  triggers   every keystroke in the search field
#             the field also swallows keydowns (line 876) so F2/Del
#             never reach the tree while typing.
#
#  IS THIS A START OR AN ANSWER?  grammar.ab (a)/(b) says a start:
#  each keystroke is its OWN act and re-fires the SAME sentence.
#  Compare rename, where typing is part of a suspended step — the
#  difference is that rename commits once, on Enter, while search
#  has no commit.  there is nothing to wait for.
#
#  so: one sentence, fired per key, each firing runs the program
#  once and halts.  no loop, no self-goto.  v4 agrees — the handler
#  sets state.query and calls renderTree() and returns.
#
#  `empty` is a real result, not an error: v4 line 350-355 swaps the
#  tree body for "No matching files" when the filter matches nothing
#  but a query is present.  it still goes to Redraw, because the
#  empty state is drawn by the same paint as the full tree.

program UserSearchesTree

sentence  User Search Tree
enter     tree.search.requested

step system search tree
  catch tree.search.ok     goto Redraw
  catch tree.search.empty  goto Redraw
